      "evidence": "template/scripts/machine_pool.py read_holders: `_try_lock(fd, path, shared=True)` then `fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)`. _try_take_slots uses LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB, which fails against a shared lock. The effect is bounded because the waiter retries on its next poll (1s), and `status` is documented as read-only. Delay of one poll only; no correctness loss.",
      "id": "holder-probe-transient-slot-lock",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The read-only holder scan briefly takes a shared flock on each free slot. A head waiter that tries to take the same slot at that instant gets a spurious failure, so status and waiting reports can delay admission."
